Usage: vcpe diagnose --name <deployment> --from <service> --to webpa --client-service <name> [flags]

Shows the expected application-to-Parodus-to-WebPA path, overlays bounded source-local HTTP observations, and identifies the first confirmed failure. Active diagnostics use only the source instance's persisted loopback endpoint.

Required flags:
  --name <deployment>     Deployment containing the source and WebPA services
  --from <service>        Gateway or XB10 source service name
  --to webpa              Diagnostic target journey
  --client-service <name>  Receive-enabled libparodus service to query

Optional flags:
  --replica <index>       Zero-based source replica index; required when replicas exceed one
  --state-root <path>     Override the default state root directory
  --json                  Emit the vcpe.dev/diagnostic/v1 graph

Examples:
  vcpe diagnose --name example --from gateway --to webpa --client-service apparmor-simulator
  vcpe diagnose --name example --from xb10 --replica 0 --to webpa --json
